{
  "name": "494. A virtual key reaches a batch or a video only when it is recorded as created by that key (task ownership) [SERIAL]",
  "description": "TXE-7119. Local fixture regression, no live provider call: run with providerErrorFixture=1 against the gateway of tests/e2e/api/provider_config/provider-error-fixture.config.json, with tests/e2e/api/runners/provider-error-fixture.mjs as the only upstream. A batch, a video or an image task is created with the operator's provider key, which every virtual key on the provider shares, and is then addressed by its id alone. Before TXE-7119 a virtual key reached any task that had no creator on record: one created outside the gateway, or whose record was lost. Now a virtual key reaches a task only under an id recorded as created by that key. The provider is the OpenAI-shaped stand-in storage_uri_files (the fixture's /pp/storage), which serves a batch create, retrieve and list; its list always holds one batch no gateway request created (batch_storage_made_elsewhere). 494.1 to 494.4 create two virtual keys and a batch under the first, which then retrieves it. 494.5 is the second key: 404. 494.6 to 494.9 are the first key addressing a batch and a video with no creator on record, by retrieve, cancel and download: each is the gateway's own 404 naming the id. 494.10 and 494.11 list batches: the first key sees its batch and not the one made elsewhere, the second key sees none. 494.12 is a batch create through the OpenAI passthrough route: 403, since a task created there would not be recorded. 494.13 is the same unrecorded batch with no virtual key: forwarded, and answered by the provider (the fixture serves that id in its list only, so its own 404 is the proof the request arrived). The batch is the fixture's and is not deleted.",
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "494.1 [setup] virtual key A (creator) on the fixture's task provider",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "prerequest",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "if (pm.variables.get('providerErrorFixture') !== '1') {",
              "  pm.execution.skipRequest();",
              "  return;",
              "}",
              "pm.collectionVariables.unset('taskVkOwner'); pm.collectionVariables.unset('taskVkOwnerId');",
              "pm.collectionVariables.unset('taskBatchId');"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('the virtual key was created', function () { pm.expect(pm.response.code, pm.response.text()).to.equal(200); });",
              "var created = (pm.response.json() || {}).virtual_key || {};",
              "pm.test('it has an id and a value', function () { pm.expect(created.id, pm.response.text()).to.be.a('string').and.not.equal(''); pm.expect(created.value, pm.response.text()).to.be.a('string').and.not.equal(''); });",
              "pm.collectionVariables.set('taskVkOwner', created.value || ''); pm.collectionVariables.set('taskVkOwnerId', created.id || '');"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\"name\": \"harness-494-a-{{$guid}}\", \"provider_configs\": [{\"provider\": \"storage_uri_files\", \"weight\": 1, \"allowed_models\": [\"*\"], \"key_ids\": [\"*\"]}, {\"provider\": \"openai\", \"weight\": 1, \"allowed_models\": [\"*\"], \"key_ids\": [\"*\"]}]}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/governance/virtual-keys",
          "host": [
